        "created_at": "2012-10-10T08:47:23.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>(Funny, I just discovered that if you post a topic with a subject line that already exists, you post successfuly but are redirected to the old topic when you click on it. So here's my second try.)</p><p>I noticed that Backlash Field has been significantly nerfed in the enhanced edition by removing the 2nd paragraph. In any case, how is the original version intended to work? For reference: \"Whenever Baron Blade is delt 5 or more damage in a single turn, put the top card of the villain deck into the villain trash\".</p><p>What I'm wondering is exactly when and how often is the effect triggered, for example, if I deal BB 3 packets of damage during my turn (5 - 1 -1):</p><p>(1) It triggers once, after I deal the first packet, because I've delt 5 damage this turn.</p><p>(2) It triggers once, at the end of my turn, since I've delt 7 damage this turn.</p><p>(3) It triggers three times: after I deal the first packet (because I've delt 5 damage this turn), after the second packet (because I've now delt 6 damage this turn), and after the third packet following the same logic.</p><p>I always implicitly assumed (1), although now (3) seems more likely after thinking about it. I guess (2) is a possibily (in this case, you would only check if something happened on a turn when that turn ends) but it seems unlikely.</p><p>Thanks</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:36:22.925Z",
