        "raw": "<p>(Funny, I just discovered that if you post a topic with a subject line that already exists, you post successfuly but are redirected to the old topic when you click on it. So here&#39;s my second try.)</p><p>I noticed that Backlash Field has been significantly nerfed in the enhanced edition by removing the 2nd paragraph. In any case, how is the original version intended to work? For reference: &quot;Whenever Baron Blade is delt 5 or more damage in a single turn, put the top card of the villain deck into the villain trash&quot;.</p><p>What I&#39;m wondering is exactly when and how often is the effect triggered, for example, if I deal BB 3 packets of damage during my turn (5 - 1 -1):</p><p>(1) It triggers once, after I deal the first packet, because I&#39;ve delt 5 damage this turn.</p><p>(2) It triggers once, at the end of my turn, since I&#39;ve delt 7 damage this turn.</p><p>(3) It triggers three times: after I deal the first packet (because I&#39;ve delt 5 damage this turn), after the second packet (because I&#39;ve now delt 6 damage this turn), and after the third packet following the same logic.</p><p>I always implicitly assumed (1), although now (3) seems more likely after thinking about it. I guess (2) is a possibily (in this case, you would only check if something happened on a turn when that turn ends) but it seems unlikely.</p><p>Thanks</p>",
