      {
        "id": 40028,
        "name": "TheJayMann",
        "username": "TheJayMann",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/thejaymann/{size}/2261_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-10-10T14:46:29.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>The difference between&nbsp;Backlash Field&nbsp;and Lead from the Front is that Backlash Field was worded to trigger once the point of damage has increased to become 5 or more damage, whereas Lead from the Front is worded to trigger whenever&nbsp;a hero target would be dealt damage.&nbsp; Backlash Field&nbsp;was not worded such as \"Whenever Baron Blade is dealt damage, if he was dealt 5 or more damage this turn.\"&nbsp; Basically, there is no wording to say it triggers when damage is dealt, only when a certain amount of damage has passed, which can occur at most once (in this case, it states per turn, thus it can occur at most once per turn).</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:13:44.115Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
