      {
        "id": 40029,
        "name": "tiborvadovan",
        "username": "tiborvadovan",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/ac8455/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-10-10T15:08:30.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>(i'll keep arguing a bit, I hope you don't mind, not trolling or anything, I just like friendly rules discussions now and then)</p><p>Actually, both cards are written in the following format:</p><p>Whenever CONDITION, RESULT.</p><p>In the case of BS, CONDITION=\"Baron Blade is delt 5 or more damage in a single turn\"</p><p>In the case of LFF, CONDITION=\"A Hero target would be delt damage by a villain card\".</p><p>The fact that the condition of BS mentions 5+ dam in a turn has no bearing on the overall phrase that describes the trigger (that would be something like \"Once per turn, whenever Baron Blade is delt 5 or more damage in a single turn ...\")</p><p>Also, it does not appear to me that the condition is worded to represent a transition from less than 5 damage to 5 or more damage, it just states that 5 or more damage (period). if I'm damaged for 5, i'm damaged for 5 or more. If then I'm damaged for 8, i'm again damaged for 5 or more...</p><p>So... yeah... doesn't seem very clear cut.</p><p>I guess it's not really that important, now that it has been rewritten. But I anyway, I enjoy the discussion (sorry about that).</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
