        "raw": "<p>(i&#39;ll keep arguing a bit, I hope you don&#39;t mind, not trolling or anything, I just like friendly rules discussions now and then)</p><p>Actually, both cards are written in the following format:</p><p>Whenever CONDITION, RESULT.</p><p>In the case of BS, CONDITION=&quot;Baron Blade is delt 5 or more damage in a single turn&quot;</p><p>In the case of LFF, CONDITION=&quot;A Hero target would be delt damage by a villain card&quot;.</p><p>The fact that the condition of BS mentions 5+ dam in a turn has no bearing on the overall phrase that describes the trigger (that would be something like &quot;Once per turn, whenever Baron Blade is delt 5 or more damage in a single turn ...&quot;)</p><p>Also, it does not appear to me that the condition is worded to represent a transition from less than 5 damage to 5 or more damage, it just states that 5 or more damage (period). if I&#39;m damaged for 5, i&#39;m damaged for 5 or more. If then I&#39;m damaged for 8, i&#39;m again damaged for 5 or more...</p><p>So... yeah... doesn&#39;t seem very clear cut.</p><p>I guess it&#39;s not really that important, now that it has been rewritten. But I anyway, I enjoy the discussion (sorry about that).</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
